      "content": "1. Nervous System – Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The neuron is the structural and functional unit of the human nervous system.",
        "The central nervous system (CNS) comprises the brain and the spinal cord, serving as the central processing unit.",
        "The cerebrum is the largest part of the brain, controlling intelligence, memory, speech, and voluntary movement.",
        "Medulla oblongata regulates crucial involuntary body activities such as respiration, heart rate, and blood pressure.",
        "Sense organs contain specialized sensory receptors that process stimuli like light (eyes) and sound (ears)."
      ],
