    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Medulla Oblongata controls autonomic functions like breathing, heart rate, and coughing; damage to it can be fatal.",
        "Cerebellum is responsible for maintaining body balance and muscle coordination; alcohol directly impairs its function.",
        "Human eye retina contains Rods (for night/dim light vision) and Cones (for bright light and color vision).",
        "The human body contains 12 pairs of cranial nerves arising from the brain and 31 pairs of spinal nerves arising from the spinal cord."
      ],
      "id": "l32o3f7"
